= Academic publishing — Technical =

Digital publishing separates content hosting, metadata registration, identifier assignment, editorial workflow, peer review, versioning, licensing, indexing, preservation, and discovery into components that may be operated by different organizations.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* academic publishing ≠ peer review
* publication ≠ correctness
* publisher ≠ owner of scientific truth

== References ==
* Crossref, content registration and bibliographic metadata documentation, current resource.
* National Academies, research-integrity and scholarly-communication reports.
* UNESCO, ''Recommendation on Open Science'' (2021), scientific publication and open-science infrastructure.
